  "sigma_method": null,
  "sigma_method_note": "How `sigma` is produced: the within-cell standard error of a single 30 x 6 reference run. SR uses the binomial standard error sqrt(p(1-p)/n); AS and ASC use the within-cell sample standard deviation divided by sqrt(n). This captures task-sampling noise, which dominates at n = 14 / 10 / 6, but not run-to-run variation of the language model; the reference run is therefore made at temperature 0. Recorded as null until the run happens, so that nothing here can be mistaken for a measurement.",
  "threshold_sigma": 3.0,
  "gated_metrics": [
    "SR",
    "AS"
  ],
  "gated_metrics_note": "Only SR and AS decide pass or fail. ASC is 0 by construction for a no-skill agent and SFR has no denominator at all; both are recorded for completeness and reported by `skillshift calibrate`, but neither can fail a run.",
